# A mermaid block draws as a diagram wherever GitHub's HTML is shown: here the description, which
# ends in one, and a comment's Preview. The page's own content isn't in the accessibility tree,
# so what's drawn is checked by the tests and seen in the snaps; this proves both pages settle
# with their diagrams drawn, as `wait settled` waits for that.
wait settled
open tamarinworks/atrium#2928
wait settled
snap description

click image #doc
wait settled
scroll scroll 2 down 300
hover textarea up 11
click button "Add a comment"
wait until text ~"Comment on line"
type "```mermaid"
press return
type "flowchart TD"
press return
type "  Draft --> Preview"
press return
type "```"
click radio "Preview"
wait until radio "Preview" has value "1"
wait until AXProgressIndicator missing
wait settled
snap preview

# Back on Write the draft is as it was typed.
click radio "Write"
wait until textarea ~"Draft --> Preview"
